      "math_academy_id": "q-118910",
      "sequence_position": 1,
      "problem": "The vector $a$ is directed due west and $|a|=16.$ The vector $b$ is directed vertically up and $|b|=8.$ Find $|a+b|.$",
      "worked_solution": "We use the triangle law of addition to add the vectors $a$ and $b.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14251309/assets/b3a60238ad44009f35ea661e39a2a5c60580f0b56149d0ad372ed52461b348c5.png)\n\nNotice that we obtain a right triangle. So, we can use Pythagorean theorem as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{|a+b|}^{2} & ={|a|}^{2}+{|b|}^{2} \\\\  & ={16}^{2}+{8}^{2} \\\\  & =320\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, $|a+b|=\\sqrt{320}=8\\sqrt{5}.$",
